# CareSteps - example environment. Copy to .env and edit, or export directly.
#
# THE APP RUNS WITHOUT ANY OF THIS. With nothing set, CareSteps starts in limited
# mode: recording, viewing, statistics, the visit summary and the emergency help path
# all work. Only the free-text conversational layer changes - it falls back to a
# scripted rule set that says plainly that it is not the assistant.
#
# See docs/architecture.md for why the fallback is a first-class path.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ model (optional)
# An OpenAI-compatible chat endpoint that supports function calling.
# Base URL must point at the API root and NOT include /chat/completions.
#
# For Anthropic Claude via the official API:
#   LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.anthropic.com/v1
#   LLM_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
#   LLM_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5
#
# Fill the three values in from your own account. Nothing here is a working
# credential, and no credential is ever committed - see .gitignore.
#
LLM_BASE_URL=
LLM_API_KEY=
LLM_MODEL=

# Seconds before a model call is treated as failed. On timeout the app degrades
# automatically rather than showing an error to the user.
LLM_TIMEOUT_S=30

# How many tool-calling rounds before the orchestrator gives up and reports what it
# managed to do. Keeps a looping model from hanging the page.
LLM_MAX_TOOL_ROUNDS=4

# Force limited mode even when a model IS configured. Useful for demoing the offline
# path deliberately, and for testing, without unplugging the network.
# LLM_FORCE_DEGRADED=1

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ app
# Where the SQLite file lives. `make seed` rebuilds whatever this points at.
# CARESTEPS_DB=/absolute/path/to/caresteps.db
